<h3>Imaging Interpretation</h3>
<h4>Technical Factors</h4>
<p>A single right lateral projection of the thorax dated January 28, 2026 is available for interpretation. There are numerous prior radiographic studies available for comparison, the most recent of which is dated January 26, 2026. </p>
<h4>Imaging Findings</h4>
<p>CARDIOVASCULAR: No abnormalities<br>
MEDIASTINAL: The esophagus is diffusely mildly gas dilated and contains the previously identified balloon esophageal feeding tube with two metallic bands. The bands now are ventral to the C5 vertebral body space and the T10 vertebral body space. A metal opaque tubular structure is passing within the plane of the feeding tube within the esophagus and terminates within the stomach.<br>
PULMONARY: No abnormalities<br>
PLEURAL SPACE &amp; DIAPHRAGM: No abnormalities<br>
MUSCULOSKELETAL: No abnormalities<br>
CRANIAL ABDOMEN: No abnormalities<br>
OTHER: No abnormalities</p>
<h4>Imaging Conclusions</h4>
<p>Appropriate repositioning of the nasogastric feeding tube and balloon esophageal feeding tube.</p>
<p>AGarza/SCG<br>
Interpreted on January 28, 2026<br>
Case no: 534870</p>
