                <td colspan="1" class="eefc0a893d3ed8e972ca7fb55d508f2216  " style="overflow-x:hidden;overflow-y:hidden;">
            <div class="" style="">
                <div style="margin:2px;overflow-y:auto;width:100%;">
            <div><b>Requested By:</b> Alyssa Jenkins DVM</div>
            <div><b>Supplier:</b> VMTH SA Radiology</div>
            <div><b>Reference:</b> US4276-DR21441</div>
            SA-RAD-Catheter Exam
                                <br><strong>Images:</strong><br>
                        
        <strong>Outcome:</strong><br>
        <div class="parsedown"><p>Lab Name: Imaging<br>
Lab Category: SA Radiography<br>
Accession Number: DXSA26-020-003<br>
Order Status: Finalized<br>
Order Last Updated: 01/20/2026 1:41 PM</p>
<h4>Faculty*</h4>
<p>N</p>
<h4>House Officer*</h4>
<p>Alyssa Jenkins</p>
<h4>Student Name</h4>
<h4>Requesting Service*</h4>
<p>SA IM1</p>
<h4>Date of Procedure*</h4>
<p>2026-01-19T11:19</p>
<h4>Patient Weight (KG)*</h4>
<p>5.17</p>
<h4>Region of Interest Previously Imaged at TAMU?*</h4>
<p>( ) No</p>
<p>(X) Yes</p>
<h4>Did Referral Films / Images Arrive with Patient?*</h4>
<p>(X) No</p>
<p>( ) Yes</p>
<h4>Anesthetized*</h4>
<p>(X) No</p>
<p>( ) Yes</p>
<h4>Sedated*</h4>
<p>( ) No</p>
<p>(X) Yes</p>
<h4>Ward/Cage*</h4>
<p>Unknown</p>
<h4>Region*</h4>
<p>Thorax</p>
<h4>What is the presenting complaint?*</h4>
<p>cath placement</p>
<h4>Are there any related physical examination, lameness and/or lab abnormalities?*</h4>
<p>placment</p>
<h4>What is your working differential list?*</h4>
<p>n/a</p>
<h4>What are your clinical questions?*</h4>
<p>placement eval</p>
<h4>What treatments are currently being Administered?</h4>
<h4>Is the patient suspected to have a zoonotic diseases?*</h4>
<p>no</p>
<h4>Are there any precautions related to the patient?*</h4>
<p>none</p>
<h4>Are there any special considerations related to scheduling?</h4>
<h4>Are there any special instructions/views?*</h4>
<p>one view</p>
<p>Fields with an asterisk are required.</p>
<h4>Radiologist</h4>
<p>Christine Gremillion</p>
<h4>Interpreted By</h4>
<p>Lily Bertelsen</p>
<h3>Imaging Interpretation</h3>
<h4>Technical Factors</h4>
<h4>Imaging Findings</h4>
<p>Two views of the thorax dated January 18th, 2026 are available for interpretation. There are previous studies available for comparison, with the most recent dated January 18th, 2026.</p>
<p>Radiographic Findings:<br>
CARDIOVASCULAR: No abnormalities.<br>
PULMONARY: Minimal to mild multifocal increased bronchial markings in the caudodorsal lungs.<br>
PLEURAL: No abnormalities.<br>
MEDIASTINAL: Similar mineral opaque feeding tube that extends along the entirety of the imaged esophagus into the gastric lumen; along with two small static metal opaque rings in the cervical esophagus and more caudally in the intrathoracic esophagus.<br>
CRANIAL ABDOMEN: The peripheral heterogeneous gas pattern previously identified associated with the stomach wall is improved. A focal moderate volume of gas persists in the wall of the gastric fundus in the current study. Apparent focal flattening of the lateral aspect of the left kidney on the VD view, though multiple skin folds also summate with this region. .<br>
MUSCULOSKELETAL: No abnormalities.<br>
OTHER: No other abnormalities.</p>
<p>Conclusions:</p>
<ol>
<li>Appropriate placement of the gastric feeding tube and balloon esophageal feeding tube. </li>
<li>Improved but persistent gastric pneumatosis. This may represent benign gastric emphysema secondary to the recently acquired stomach biopsies and/or pre-existing mucosal ulceration or other mucosal trauma; in light of the improvement, emphysematous gastritis secondary to infection with gas-producing bacteria or ischemic injury are considered less likely.* Correlation with patient clinical signs would be helpful, however.</li>
<li>Minimal to mild bronchial pattern may be secondary to underlying inflammatory airway disease. </li>
<li>Possible chronic left renal infarct versus summation of a skin fold.</li>
</ol>
<p>*Thierry F, Ferreira MF, Paterson GK, Liuti T, Del-Pozo J. Canine and feline emphysematous gastritis may be differentiated from gastric emphysema based on clinical and imaging characteristics: Five cases. Vet Radiol Ultrasound. 2019 Mar;60(2):136-144.</p>
<p>LBertelsen/CGremillion<br>
Interpreted on January 20th, 2026<br>
Case no. 534870</p>
<h4>Imaging Conclusions</h4>
<h4>Comments</h4>
<p><a href="https://labs.vmth.tamu.edu/OrderRequestForm?id=18774&amp;accessToken=8575c82e-cd2b-488e-8431-684364e82e69">Click here to PACS Viewer Link</a></p></div>        <strong>Clinic Notes / Specifics:</strong><br>
        <div class="parsedown"><p>one view placement</p></div><br>
                
