<h4>Pertinent History</h4>
<p>The patient has a lifelong history of vomiting 1-4 times monthly with increasing frequency of regurgitation episodes. Intestinal muscularis thickening noted on AUS. Recently hospitalized for lily ingestion with refractory regurgitation; re-hospitalized. Found to have severe esophageal stricture near the thoracic inlet. BE tube placed. Pt has been on esomeprazole, cisapride, metoclopramide, antiemetics. Histo EIA &amp; GI panel pending. </p>
