            <div class="" style="">
                <div style="margin:2px;overflow-y:auto;width:100%;">
            <div><b>Requested By:</b> Anvita (Vida) Hanchate DVM</div>
            <div><b>Supplier:</b> VMTH SA Ultrasound</div>
            <div><b>Reference:</b> US4276-DR16527</div>
            SA-US-GI Focus
                                <br><strong>Images:</strong><br>
                        
        <strong>Outcome:</strong><br>
        <div class="parsedown"><p>Lab Name: Imaging<br>
Lab Category: SA Ultrasound<br>
Accession Number: USSA26-001-003<br>
Order Status: Finalized<br>
Order Last Updated: 01/14/2026 12:06 PM</p>
<h4>Faculty*</h4>
<p>Yankin</p>
<h4>House Officer*</h4>
<p>Vida</p>
<h4>Student Name</h4>
<h4>Requesting Service*</h4>
<p>SA CC</p>
<h4>Date of Procedure*</h4>
<p>2025-01-01T14:07</p>
<h4>Patient Weight (KG)*</h4>
<p>6.8</p>
<h4>Region of Interest Previously Imaged at TAMU?*</h4>
<p>( ) No</p>
<p>(X) Yes</p>
<h4>Did Referral Films / Images Arrive with Patient?*</h4>
<p>( ) No</p>
<p>(X) Yes</p>
<h4>Anesthetized*</h4>
<p>(X) No</p>
<p>( ) Yes</p>
<h4>Sedated*</h4>
<p>( ) No</p>
<p>(X) Yes</p>
<h4>Ward/Cage*</h4>
<p>1012B-10 - 1012B ER Ward</p>
<h4>Region*</h4>
<p>Thorax/Abdomen</p>
<h4>What is the presenting complaint?*</h4>
<p>lily ingestion</p>
<h4>Are there any related physical examination, lameness and/or lab abnormalities?*</h4>
<p>r+, large stomach</p>
<h4>What is your working differential list?*</h4>
<p>evidence of pyloric obstruction</p>
<h4>What are your clinical questions?*</h4>
<p>evidence of pyloric obstruction</p>
<h4>What treatments are currently being administered?</h4>
<p>x</p>
<h4>Is the patient suspected to have a zoonotic diseases?*</h4>
<p>x</p>
<h4>Are there any precautions related to the patient?*</h4>
<p>x</p>
<h4>Are there any special considerations related to scheduling?</h4>
<p>x</p>
<h4>Are there any special instructions/views?</h4>
<p>x</p>
<p>Fields with an asterisk are required.</p>
<h4>Senior Clinician</h4>
<p>Sam Glamann</p>
<h4>Interpreted By</h4>
<p>Sarah Sampson</p>
<h3>Imaging Interpretation</h3>
<h4>Technical Factors</h4>
<p>Focused gastrointestinal ultrasound (28 still images and 2 cineloops) performed on January 1, 2026. There are no previous studies available for comparison.</p>
<h4>Imaging Findings</h4>
<p>STOMACH: The stomach contains a large amount of heterogeneously echogenic fluid with maintenance of normal wall thickness and layering.<br>
SMALL INTESTINES: The duodenum has minimal content with normal wall thickness and layering. The jejunum and ileum have multifocal moderate muscularis layering thickness with maintenance of normal wall layering.<br>
COLON: The colon contains hyperechoic shadowing gas and maintains normal wall thickness and layering.<br>
LYMPH NODES: Some jejunal lymph nodes are mildly enlarged, rounded, and hypoechoic, estimated up to 7.4 mm in width.<br>
OTHER: None. </p>
<h4>Imaging Conclusions</h4>
<ol>
<li>Severe gastric distension and moderate, multifocal small intestinal muscularis thickening. These gastrointestinal findings are consistent with gastroenterocolitis and associated delayed pyloric outflow and ileus. The jejunal muscularis thickening is most consistent with a chronic enteropathy, such as inflammatory bowel disease or small cell GI lymphoma. There is no evidence of gastrointestinal obstruction.</li>
<li>Jejunal lymphadenopathy is consistent with reactive hyperplasia related to #1. However, infiltrative neoplasia (round cell) cannot be ruled out. </li>
</ol>
<p>SSampson/SCG<br>
January 1, 2026<br>
CASE# 534870</p>
