                                <br><strong>Images:</strong><br>
                        
        <strong>Outcome:</strong><br>
        <div class="parsedown"><p>Lab Name: Imaging<br>
Lab Category: SA Radiography<br>
Accession Number: DXSA26-002-001<br>
Order Status: Finalized<br>
Order Last Updated: 01/02/2026 2:10 PM</p>
<h4>Faculty*</h4>
<p>Anvita Hanchate</p>
<h4>House Officer*</h4>
<h4>Student Name</h4>
<h4>Requesting Service*</h4>
<p>SA CC</p>
<h4>Date of Procedure*</h4>
<p>2025-01-01T15:51</p>
<h4>Patient Weight (KG)*</h4>
<p>6.8</p>
<h4>Region of Interest Previously Imaged at TAMU?*</h4>
<p>( ) No</p>
<p>(X) Yes</p>
<h4>Did Referral Films / Images Arrive with Patient?*</h4>
<p>(X) No</p>
<p>( ) Yes</p>
<h4>Anesthetized*</h4>
<h4>Sedated*</h4>
<h4>Ward/Cage*</h4>
<p>Unknown</p>
<h4>Region*</h4>
<p>Thorax</p>
<h4>What is the presenting complaint?*</h4>
<p>NGT placement check</p>
<h4>Are there any related physical examination, lameness and/or lab abnormalities?*</h4>
<h4>What is your working differential list?*</h4>
<p>n/a</p>
<h4>What are your clinical questions?*</h4>
<p>tube placement?</p>
<h4>What treatments are currently being Administered?</h4>
<h4>Is the patient suspected to have a zoonotic diseases?*</h4>
<h4>Are there any precautions related to the patient?*</h4>
<p>none</p>
<h4>Are there any special considerations related to scheduling?</h4>
<h4>Are there any special instructions/views?*</h4>
<p>Fields with an asterisk are required.</p>
<h4>Radiologist</h4>
<p>Jay Griffin</p>
<h4>Interpreted By</h4>
<h3>Imaging Interpretation</h3>
<h4>Technical Factors</h4>
<p>Thorax (3 images):</p>
<h4>Imaging Findings</h4>
<p>A tube extends through the esophagus and terminates in the gastric cardia.  The esophagus is moderately gas dilated.  The heart and pulmonary vessels are normal in size and shape.  There is a mild diffuse interstitial lung pattern.  There is mild retraction of the right lungs from the thoracic body wall with rounding of the right costophrenic recess.  The trachea and mainstem bronchi are normal in size and shape.  The visible portion of the skeleton and cranial abdomen is normal.</p>
<h4>Imaging Conclusions</h4>
<p>1: Esophageal tube placement.<br>
2: Suspected small volume right sided pleural effusion.  The underlying cause is not seen.<br>
3: The mild diffuse interstitial lung pattern is probably caused by atelectasis associated with sedation for the esophageal tube placement.</p>
<h4>Comments</h4>
<p><a href="https://labs.vmth.tamu.edu/OrderRequestForm?id=15833&amp;accessToken=e1ddeff4-7f0e-4cca-9358-c4d37e8283a5">Click here to PACS Viewer Link</a></p></div>        <strong>Clinic Notes / Specifics:</strong><br>
        <div class="parsedown"><p>NGT placement check</p></div><br>
                
        </div></div>
